        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Assault 5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c">Any rolls to wound of a 6 count as AP1. Special Issue</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Advanced Stabilisation System" id="b65a-f5a5-5a41-daf6" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">During the Movement Phase, the battlesuit may choose to use the Slow and Purposeful universal special rule for the remainder of the turn, though if it does it may not make an additional jetpack move in the Assault phase.


If one model in a team has this wargear, then all models in the team must be similarly equipped. If one model makes use of the system, all must do so. The unit may still take drones.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Blacksun Filter" id="f235-7880-f61b-f7d2" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">This equipment enables the bearer to double the distance rolled for determining how far they can see when fighting at night. Only models equipped with the Blacksun filter gain this benefit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Bonding Knife" id="8917-b687-41df-907b" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">So long as the bearer is alive, the squad may regroup even if below half strength.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Command and Control Node" id="7d09-1c37-fac3-3e7e" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">All friendly units with a model within 12" may use the bearer's Leadership for the purposes of Target Priority tests.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Drone Controller" id="6a48-ae3b-b476-9d71" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A model with a drone controller must take one or two Gun, Marker or Shield Drones, in any combination.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Ejection Systems" id="a713-821a-1b43-d6f1" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Should the character lose his last wound to a shooting attack that does not cause Instant Death, the battlesuit is replaced with a single model, representing the pilot.


The profile of this model is the same as before the pilot ejected, less 2 Strength, 1 Toughness and it has 1 Wound and no Armour Save. It is equipped with a pulse pistol only. Independent characters and single-member teams ('Monats') without drones only.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Failsafe Detonator" id="8e65-c1e1-0547-4206" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The failsafe detonator may be triggered if the bearer is part of a team that is forced to make a Fall Back move having lost an assault.


The team is moved as normal, but the character stays where he is and the enemy may not make a Sweeping Advance. Once his team has moved, and before Pile in moves, the character activates the detonator - Place the Large Blast marker centred on the character, and roll for partial hits on the other models as normal. Every model hit takes a single, Strength 8, AP- hit, and the character is removed as a casualty. The enemy may not consolidate. Note that the enemy unit need not take a Morale check should this attack inflict 25% casualties, as it occurs outside the normal sequence in which such checks are required.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Iridium Armour Plates" id="210b-c88e-ce5c-fabd" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer's Armour Save is increased to 2+, but the additional 6" move in the Assault phase is reduced to D6"</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Multi-tracker" id="f2d8-73a2-483f-7625" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">This wargear allows the bearer to fire two battlesuit weapon systems in the same turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Positional Relay" id="7faf-215a-ae41-d28e" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">From the second turn onwards, as long as the bearer is on the table at the beginning of the turn in which this device is used, a single unit that is being held in Reserve may be deployed on a D6 roll of 2+, though no other units in Reserve may be deployed this turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Shield Generator" id="aed5-b40c-b40b-dfb4" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The shield generator confers a 4+ Invulnerable save to the bearer</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Stealth Field Generator" id="4140-e781-09d4-8186" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Enemy models attempting to fire at a unit wholly equipped with stealth field generators must roll to check their spotting distance by rolling 2D6x3 as if firing at night. If the models are not within spotting range, the firer may not choose to fire at a different target. The firing unit may, however choose to ignore models equipped with stealth field generators and fire on a more distant target, and in this case will not benefit from cover by the unit. If firing at models equipped with stealth field generators while the Night Fighting special rule is in effect, no further effect is gained. Barrage weapons roll an additional D6 for scatter when targeting a model equipped with a stealth field generator. Any drones controlled by a model with a stealth field generator will also be shielded at no further cost in points.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Stimulant Injector" id="cac3-0c54-a85b-59a4" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer has the Feel no Pain special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Target Lock" id="acc9-9396-2894-6426" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer may target a seperate enemy unit to that engated by the rest of its own unit. All firing in the unit must be declared before any to hit rolls are made.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Targeting Array" id="3c84-bbba-a8c2-fdc0" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A targeting array grants the user +1 BS, up to BS 5.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Vectored retro-thrusters" id="ba1a-533b-aa8b-c276" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer benefits from the Hit and Run universal special rule. Indipendent characters and single-member teams ('monats') without drones only.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="EMP Grenades" id="3d70-3805-5ae7-8c36" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">EMP Grenades are used when assaulting enemy vehicles, hitting in the same way as grenades and melta bombs. When determining damage, roll a D6. On a 4 or 5 they inflict a glancing hit, on a 6 they inflict a penetrating hit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Honour Blade" id="1688-3488-96d6-ecc0" hidden="false" typeId="1d88-1369-f0ed-b39c" typeName="Melee Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Ability" typeId="2113-98a2-4376-a94c">The Honour Blade must be used in two hands - the wielder cannot therefore count as carrying an additional weapon. It adds +2 to the wielder's Strength.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Networked Markerlight" id="ebf0-1674-f193-5618" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Unlike a normal markerlight, the operator's own unit may benefit from its use. It is fired before the remainder of the unit fires. All other rules given for the basic markerlight apply. For example, a Marker Drone is equipped with a networked markerlight, meaning that models in the same unit may expend counters placed as a result of its own shooting.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Photon Grenades" id="7ace-3a5d-d7a5-765a" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Models charging against units equipped with photon grenades gain no bonus attacks for charging, but still employ any special close combat attacks they gain when charging.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Decoy launchers" id="b563-0d07-491d-9e02" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Whenever a glancing hit causes an Immobilised result onto the vehicle, the Tau player may force his opponent to re-roll the dice, and the second result applies.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Disruption pod" id="4a46-c486-93e8-22cd" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Weapons firing at the vehicle from more than 12" distant count the vehicle as an Obscured Target</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Flechette Discharger" id="5980-b148-b086-932e" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Any model attacking the vehicle in close combat will be wounded on a D6 roll of 4+, with Saves allowed, before resolving its attacks.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Gun Drones" id="bc64-e7df-1cfd-918b" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The vehicle may be equipped with two Gun Drones. The drones will move with the vehicle, safely contained in specially designed recesses. During any Tau Movement Phase, the drones may disengage in the same way as infantry dismount from a transport and form an independent unit. From then on, the drones function as a Drone squadron. The drones may not rejoin the vehicle during a game and will never count as a Scoring Unit. 


While attached, the Gun Drones may fire as part of the vehicle, using their own BS, in addition to any other weapons that would normally be permitted to fire, and are treated as passengers if the vehicle is damaged.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Landing Gear" id="8c9b-75cc-c314-355b" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">In any turn that the vehicle does not move, it may choose to no longer count as a Skimmer until it moves again. This benefit does not apply on the first turn of the game.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Vehicle-mounted Multi-tracker" id="9887-af37-eca1-27c5" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The vehicle-mounted multi-tracker is combined with advanced stabilisers enabling a vehicle to fire as if it were a fast vehicle.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Sensor Spines" id="b56a-b649-de8c-8eac" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The vehicle may opt to use Sensor Spines instead of moving normally. Whilst doing so, the vehicle does not hover above a terrain feature - instead, it is counted as actually moving through it. It may therefore claim to be an obscured target in the same way as a normal vehicle in the same position, but the sensors allow it to avoid the effects of dangerous terrain.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Vehicle-mounted Target Lock" id="58a3-e56f-4a63-2553" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Each weapon on the vehicle may fire at a seperate enemy if desired, subject to the normal line of sight rules.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Pulse Carbine" id="38bc-4e53-be82-6233" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">18"</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Assault 1, Pinning, Twin-linked</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c" />
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Honour Guard Shas'la" id="a5a6-65b2-033e-0f52" hidden="false" typeId="0967-823d-dd82-4e47" typeName="Unit">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="15b1-a34a-6e7c-332e">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="63a5-4be2-9cc0-7723">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="09af-e927-0c3c-9d88">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ff29-f8b2-5b20-b686">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="4a81-ac45-a71c-c71e">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="8517-a46c-d6df-9c75">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="a535-0722-3bc1-4d3c">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="ddd5-77eb-4cc8-9eab">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="c1e7-f1bd-8acd-7595">4+</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Honour Guard Shas'ui" id="c5f2-e947-65d7-513e" hidden="false" typeId="0967-823d-dd82-4e47" typeName="Unit">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="15b1-a34a-6e7c-332e">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="63a5-4be2-9cc0-7723">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="09af-e927-0c3c-9d88">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ff29-f8b2-5b20-b686">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="4a81-ac45-a71c-c71e">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="8517-a46c-d6df-9c75">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="a535-0722-3bc1-4d3c">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="ddd5-77eb-4cc8-9eab">8</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="c1e7-f1bd-8acd-7595">4+</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Railgun (Solid Shot)" id="082b-7c71-bb05-2c50" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">72"</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">10</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c" />
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Burst Cannon" id="14a6-183c-b723-cc30" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">18"</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Assault 3, Twin-linked</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c" />
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles><sharedRules><rule name="Recoil Absorption" id="2f0f-299b-863e-1fb1" hidden="false">
      <description>All XV battlesuits are designed to compensate for the recoil of light weapons fire, so they do not count as moving when they fire rapid fire weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Improved Sensors" id="81fc-e040-2ca5-aa59" hidden="false">
      <description>Crisis, Stealth, and Broadside battlesuits are equipped with a number of variable spectrum sensors and scanners. These sensors allow them to detech ambushes or Lictors using secret deployment. One member of the team may scan instead of shooting during the Shooting phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jetpack" id="489d-ec6a-0dcb-d81f" hidden="false">
      <description>Tau jetpacks are extremely agile, combining anti-gravitic and jet technology. A model with a jetpack can either:
- Move 6" in their Movement phase, ignoring intervening terrain as they fly over it like a model with a jump pack;
- Move up to 6" by walking or hovering just above the ground as normal infantry.
They will also fall back and sweeping advance 3D6".
Troops equipped with jetpacks may Deep Strike when the mission permits.
An unbroken model with a jetpack that is not in close combat may always move 6" in the Assault phase whether they are with 6" of an enemy or not. This move may be in any direction. It does not have to be a charge towards the enemy, even if the jetpack wearer is within 6" of an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealthsuit" id="5519-d934-3cfb-7a6a" hidden="false">
      <description>Stealthsuits incorporate a holographic disruption field that makes it wearer hard to spot. Enemy models attempting to fire at Stealth armor troops count as if firing at night and must roll to check their spotting distance. 


If the Stealthsuit troopers are not within spotting range the unit misses its chance to fire while searching for a target and so may not choose a different target. 


Stealthsuit troopers count as being in cover if they are assaulted, but not if they charge. If firing at Stealthsuits while the Night Fighting scenario special rules are in effect, the rolled spotting distance is halved.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sensor - Multi-tracker" id="6061-4fc4-3974-c586" hidden="false">
      <description>The multi-tracker enables the suit wearer to fire two Crisis or Broadsuit battlesuit weapon systems.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sensor - Target Lock" id="787b-9a81-c4e0-ee02" hidden="false">
      <description>The target lock enables the model to target a separate enemy unit to that engaged by the rest of its own unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shield Generator" id="b433-5621-8ff1-e373" hidden="false">
      <description>This confers a 4+ Invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone Controller" id="56e7-a13f-c004-e8dd" hidden="false">
      <description>A drone controller enables the suit wearer to command from 1 to 2 gun or sheild drones.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Honour Blade" id="e4b3-561f-f686-b18d" hidden="false">
      <description>The honour blade is a two-handed weapon that cannot be used with an additional weapon. It adds +2 S to the wielder's Strength when rolling to wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bonding Knife" id="1f5f-2d35-c5f7-9db4" hidden="false">
      <description>A bonded team may regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blacksun Filter" id="da14-cfd0-1939-ad50" hidden="false">
      <description>Enables the user to see up to 4D6 x 3" when fighting at night.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Decoy Launchers" id="e807-f290-815c-7312" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever a Glancing Hit result of 4 (Immobilised) is rolled against the vehicle, the decoy launchers force the damage dice to be re-rolled, but the re-rolled result stands.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disruption Pod" id="2f77-21e2-5667-f96d" hidden="false">
      <description>Weapons firing at a vehicle equiped with a Disruption Pod reduce their range by 6", down to a minimum of 24" or the maximum range of the weapon, whichever is less.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flechette Discharger" id="fe8d-2fa4-d273-0725" hidden="false">
      <description>If an enemy model elects to make a death or glory attempt during a tank shock by a vehicle equipped with flechette dischargers, it must first pass an Armour saving throw or suffer one wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Multi-tracker" id="28ca-eea0-3317-daf9" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle-mounted multi-tracker allows the vehicle to fire as if it were a fast vehicle. Therefore it can fire one weapon if moving up to 12" and all weapons if moving up to 6".</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Seeker Missiles" id="3da4-d1a8-b8ae-b4ad" hidden="false">
      <description>Any model equipped with a markerlight may request a single missile to be launched if they score a hit on the desired target with their markerlight. The missles do not need a line of sight from the vehicle to the target, and they hit on a 2+. Against vehicles, the missle strikes the armour facing the firing vehicle, even if the markerlight is in a different facing. The target can still use the benefits of cover they are in or immediately behind.
The vehicle equipped with the missiles cannot launch them itself. They are always fired by other models armed with markerlights.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sensor Spines" id="facc-db84-ec11-bf2c" hidden="false">
      <description>Sensor spines allow the vehicle to detect ambushes (Codex: Catachans, p.20) and secret deployments (Lictors, Codex: Tyranids, p.11). They may shoot and scan in the same Shooting Phase. Additionally, a vehicle fitted with sensor spines will only trigger a mine when passing over a minefield on a roll of 6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Target Lock" id="83bc-f6e9-89c3-4bf3" hidden="false">
      <description>The target lock enables the model to target a separate enemy unit with each weapon, if desired.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Targetting Array" id="ce5a-d3df-81a4-b045" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 BS to the vehicle.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules><sharedSelectionEntries><selectionEntry name="Shas'el" id="b044-07fe-a372-df49" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="HQ" id="b131-7eb7-6547-a9e5" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="ac8d-efba-1884-d3ad" />
        <categoryLink name="Independent Character" id="b950-f0dd-8acb-6b41" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="3c96-248b-affd-e504" />
        <categoryLink name="Infantry" id="e551-2ca1-98e3-285e" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="6953-6bba-0bb9-d49d" />
