    <selectionEntry name="Kroot Carnivore Squad" id="4a6e-34f4-77b7-2ab9" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Troops" id="d273-6b10-745c-33d6" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="default-category" />
        <categoryLink name="Infantry" id="6b82-34c2-002a-2c9a" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="6953-6bba-0bb9-d49d" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Infiltrators" id="d694-147a-5ff4-9d75" hidden="false" targetId="b4ea-750c-d9a4-e398" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="02dc-e73d-f9f7-357a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Mercenaries" id="17cb-dfc2-d32b-4121" hidden="false">
          <description>The leadership of the Kroot is not fixed, instead is considered equal to their points value. Normally it is 7, but if they are upgraded with a 6+ Armor save it increeases to 8. Note that the presence of a Kroot Shaper, Kroot Hounds or a Krootox doesn't directly affect the Leadership of the squad.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Eaters of the Dead" id="ded2-3151-7ce0-dbc5" hidden="false">
          <description>Kroot must pass a Leadership test in order to pursue a foe defeated in close combat or make a sweeping advance. If the test is failed the Kroot must instead consolidate. If a Kroot Shaper is in the squad then they MUST consolidate, they have no choice.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Fieldcraft" id="91cd-ebc7-b892-3f86" hidden="false">
          <description>Kroot gain +1 to their cover save in woods or jungles. Kroot in woods or jungles do not roll a Difficult Terrain test; they may always move up to 6". If they do not move in the movement phase they may see and shoot through 12" of woods or jungle terrain rather than the normal 6"</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="6+ Armor" id="9cc8-cef8-79e3-3a0e" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="a11c-217a-1221-ff93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
