    <selectionEntry name="Gue'vesa Team (Chapter Approved)" id="2127-779a-69aa-5d70" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <comment>http://uk.games-workshop.com/40kuniverse/warhammer40k/Chapter_Approved/assets/Tau_human_auxileries.pdf</comment>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Troops" id="8c98-f221-ad50-cf5c" primary="true" targetId="default-category" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="e6d5-bc03-5827-d5da" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="0" />
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Traitors" id="1a07-0288-1bcc-259c" hidden="false">
          <description>Although the humans who have joined the Tau empire bear no ill-will towards their former compatriots, the same cannot be said of Imperial troops fighting the auxiliaries. Imperial troops (Space Machines, Imperial Guard, Witch Hunters, Daemon Hunters, etc.) will always hit Gue'vesa on a roll of 3+ in close combat, regardless of relative Weapon Skill.</description>
        </rule>
